                      %a{:href => "/nlab/edit/differential+cohomology+-+contents"} Edit this sidebar
          %p This entry is about the article
          %ul
            %li#KahleValentino
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Kahle"}> Alexander Kahle
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alessandro+Valentino"} Alessandro Valentino
              = succeed "," do
                %em T-duality and Differential K-Theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0912.2516"} arXiv:0912.2516
          %p
            on the identification of the correct description in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
            and
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+K-theory"} differential K-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-duality
            or
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+T-duality"} topological T-duality
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+T-duality"} differential T-duality
          %p A review is in section 7.4 of
          %ul
            %li#BunkeSchick
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Schick"} Thomas Schick
              %em Differential K-theory. A survey
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1011.6663"}> arXiv:1011.6663
              ).
          %p We try to indicate some of the content. There are two main ingredients:
          %ul
            %li
              a
              %a{:href => "#FormalizationOfTheSetup"} formalization of the setup
          %p
            which proposes a refinement of the ingredients of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+T-duality"} topological T-duality
            to
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#StatementOfDifferentialTduality"}> statement of differential T-duality
              ,
          %p
            which is the assertion that this setup naturally induces the T-duality operation as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+differential+K-theory"} twisted differential K-theory
          %h2#FormalizationOfTheSetup Formalization of the setup
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Λ
                  %mo ⊂
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda \subset \mathbb{R}^n
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice"} lattice
            (a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete
            subgroup of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real number
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+product"} cartesian power
          %p Write
          .maruku-equation
